{"title":"2017 CEMC CTMC Problems/Relay 0 Problem C","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Relay_0_Problem_C&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" /> be TNYWR.<br />\nIn the diagram, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> is isosceles with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/4/5f4c25cb7b6078137512af0317bd262160bd0319.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=BC$\" width=\"81\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Relay_0_Problem_C&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/8/b68a4f91a94d7c0bab6030e376aff8d2fd074960.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BAC = t^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"96\" height=\"15\" />, what is the measure of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/a/a3ad57710b6810476e6017ea2c2cc6d41219c218.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"57\" height=\"14\" />, in degrees?  \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Relay_0_Problem_C&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/7/fb71d5ba363a314c0343efdd9a19aafe8070c75e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = BC$\" width=\"81\" height=\"13\" /> in the triangle, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/2/56233c1298cf11d5c7b5fd2186445c0a05adb197.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m \\angle BAC = m \\angle ACB = t^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"207\" height=\"15\" />. The sum of the interior angles in any <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Triangle\" title=\"Triangle\">triangle</a> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/0/3f0cd95f95238159d02dbcea0aca632c2928991c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$180^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"37\" height=\"15\" />, so we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/2/4e2a1abd52a8117bfdde7acbf1e320982ac955ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m \\angle BAC + m \\angle ACB + m \\angle ABC = 180^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"320\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/6/b8687ab7a48367cf065450ef0fbd80d97a22a568.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t^{\\circ} + t^{\\circ} + m \\angle ABC = 180^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"205\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/8/ff802b4970793d5e9f817304ec9099a90c5632fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m \\angle ABC = (180 - 2t)^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"184\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>From <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Relay_0_Problem_B\" title=\"2017 CEMC CTMC Problems/Relay 0 Problem B\">seat B</a>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/2/142c1f2c693b3b99ee31849eb9ce5c622515e74a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t = 70^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"58\" height=\"15\" />. Plugging this into what we have, we get:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/d/7bdaa02e00b314e4e6c307fe3faae9d79bacf582.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m \\angle ABC = (180 - 2 \\times 70)^{\\circ} = (180 - 140)^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"341\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/6/166bdb4519ce005cfcc2cb3575666f76e00de1a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=\\boxed{40^{\\circ}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"58\" height=\"26\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_CTMC\" title=\"2017 CEMC CTMC\">2017 CEMC CTMC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_CTMC_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2017 CEMC CTMC Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_CTMC_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2017 CEMC CTMC Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Relay_0_Problem_B\" title=\"2017 CEMC CTMC Problems/Relay 0 Problem B\">Relay 0 Problem B</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Relay_1_Problem_A\" title=\"2017 CEMC CTMC Problems/Relay 1 Problem A\">Relay 1 Problem A</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Individual_Problem_1\" titl